{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>With the lips.</b> And not in the heart (ibid.)." "<b>To do harm.</b> To himself." "<b>Or to do good.</b> To himself — for example, 'I will eat,' 'I will not eat'; 'I will sleep,' 'I will not sleep' (Shevuot 27)." "<b>To all that a person utters.</b> To include what has already passed." "<b>And it was hidden from him.</b> And he transgressed his oath. All of these are in a graduated offering, as explained here; but an oath involving denial of money is not in this offering but in an asham."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:01.996799671Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}